,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":139.612081226,"data":"Problem: A train departs with 100 passengers. At the first stop, 20 leave and 35 enter. How many passengers now?\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":139.612086156,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":139.612090604,"data":"[SymboLM Generation]\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":143.281339509,"data":"Okay, so I'm trying to figure out how many passengers are on the train after the first stop. Let me start by breaking down the problem step by step. \r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":143.281453809,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":145.322527649,"data":"First, the train departs with 100 passengers. That's straightforward. So, at the start, there are 100 people on board. \r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":145.322565884,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":148.181791037,"data":"Now, at the first stop, some passengers get off and others get on. Specifically, 20 passengers leave the train, and 35 new passengers board. I need to calculate the total number of passengers after these changes.\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":148.181828734,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":151.650922213,"data":"Let me think about this. When passengers leave, the number of passengers decreases, and when new passengers board, the number increases. So, I should subtract the 20 who got off from the initial 100, and then add the 35 who got on.\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":151.650964205,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":154.505585013,"data":"So, starting with 100 passengers, subtracting 20 gives me 80 passengers remaining after the first stop. Then, adding 35 passengers would bring the total to 115 passengers on the train.\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":154.505625785,"data":"\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":156.695612325,"data":"Wait, let me double-check that. 100 minus 20 is indeed 80, and 80 plus 35 is 115.\r\n"}
,{"stream_name":"stdout","time":156.69565745,"data":"\r\n"}
